    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d372">

                <pb facs="d372-1" n="1" xml:id="d372-1"/>

                <head>372. Memorandum From the President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs
                    (Kissinger) to the Acting Secretary of Defense and the Director of Central
                    Intelligence (Schlesinger), Washington, June 18, 1973.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d372-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d372-f2"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline>
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1973-06-18">June 18, 1973</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>THE WHITE HOUSE<lb/>WASHINGTON</p>
                <p>June 18, 1973</p>
                <p>MEMORANDUM FOR<lb/>THE ACTING SECRETARY OF DEFENSE<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >text not declassified</hi>]</p>
                <p>SUBJECT: Thai SGU Program, FY 1974</p>
                <p>The memorandum of May 10 from the Secretary of Defense on this subject has been
                    reviewed. In light of the considerations raised therein, the plan to maintain 17
                    battalions during the first half of Fiscal Year 1974 and 10 battalions in the
                    second half should be implemented using the [<hi rendition="#italic">text not
                        declassified</hi>]. Action to withdraw the Thai SGUs from Laos should not be
                    taken until further advised.</p>
                <p>Henry A. Kissinger [signed]</p>
                <p>cc: The Secretary of State</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d372-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d372-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, Nixon Presidential Materials, NSC Files, Box 565,
                    Country Files, Far East, Thailand, Volume 10, 1973–. Secret; Sensitive. The
                    Secretary of State also received a copy of this memorandum.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d372-f2" n="2" xml:id="d372-f2-content">
                <p>Kissinger directed the DOD to fund the Thai Special Guerrilla Units during the
                    1974 fiscal year.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
